    "quotes": [
      "Known phyla, unknown proteome: a controlled census of the Rub' al-Khali soil metagenome",
      "The initial screen used both PDB and AlphaFold references; the paired experiment used a newer PDB snapshot and greater retrieval depth. These changes allow whole-chain classifications to differ between panels a and b.",
      "Removing CPU rows with out-of-range alignment scores left the primary whole-chain and crop match classifications unchanged; stricter exclusion tiers changed whole-chain classifications for four distinct control models and crop classifications for nine distinct control models.",
      "We selected one locus per family and species by descending complete-window eligibility, first for exact-coordinate windows and then for the same-strand stop-match sensitivity. Ties used descending counts of exact-mapped, exact-or-stop-mapped and present flanks, followed by contig length and gene count, then ascending member identifier.",
      "Each stratum's weight was the product of its two group sizes divided by its total size",
      "The same-class comparison retained 236 genomes, excluding the single Thermoplasmata representative whose primary comparator belonged to SW-10-69-26.",
      "Cropping jointly changes sequence extent, score normalisation and search opportunity.",
      "the public filereport returned zero runs on 13 October 2026. The recorded release date is 1 November 2026; public release or reviewer access remains to be confirmed before submission",
      "A MAG deposition with MIMAG metadata and an archived release DOI are pending",
      "complete raw-to-final reproduction is limited by 78 missing raw-file paths, 302 permission failures, unverified duplicate-run merge commands and incomplete historical claim-registry migration. These are documented submission prerequisites.",
      "The complete analysis table rebuilds byte-for-byte from the preserved metadata, laboratory and climate summary tables; regenerating the original climate retrieval is a separate provenance gap",
      "flanking annotation opportunity above versus at or below the pooled median",
